'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\v4.0.30319\\Config'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'machine.config'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to 'count(/configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled) = 0 or /configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled = \"true\"'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.dotnet:ste:900 (xmlfilecontent_state)\nState Comment           : enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled = false\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value_of' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework\\v4.0.30319\\Config\\machine.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework\\v4.0.30319\\Config'\n                        : filename equals 'machine.config'\n                        : xpath equals 'count(/configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled) = 0 or /configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled = \"true\"'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\v4.0.30319\\Config\\machine.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\v4.0.30319\\Config'\n                        : filename equals 'machine.config'\n                        : xpath equals 'count(/configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled) = 0 or /configuration/runtime/enforceFIPSPolicy/@enabled = \"true\"'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","group_tree":{"id":"V-225230","title":"SRG-APP-000635"},"rule_version":"APPNET0062","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Examine the .NET CLR configuration files to find the runtime element and then the \"enforceFIPSPolicy\" element.\n\nExample:\n&lt;configuration&gt; \n  &lt;runtime&gt; \n                &lt;enforceFIPSPolicy enabled=\"true|false\" /&gt;\n  &lt;/runtime&gt;\n&lt;/configuration&gt;\n\nDelete the \"enforceFIPSPolicy\" runtime element, change the setting to \"true\" or there must be documented IAO approvals for the FIPS setting.","ia_controls":""},{"weight":"10.0","status":"open","rule_version":"APPNET0063","group_tree":{"id":"V-225231","title":"SRG-APP-000175"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:54\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Verify registry key for 64 bit version of .NET must be configured to validate strong names on full-trust assemblies.)\nTest                    :   false (Verify registry key for 32 bit version of .NET must be configured to validate strong names on full-trust assemblies.)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework\\AllowStrongNameBypass'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523101 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify registry key for 64 bit version of .NET must be configured to validate strong names on full-trust assemblies.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523101 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Registry key for 64 bit .NetFramework AllowStrongNameBypass\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowStrongNameBypass'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523101 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework'\n                        : name equals 'AllowStrongNameBypass'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055496430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523102 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify registry key for 32 bit version of .NET must be configured to validate strong names on full-trust assemblies.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523102 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Registry key for 32 bit .NetFramework AllowStrongNameBypass\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowStrongNameBypass'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523101 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework\\AllowStrongNameBypass'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","fix_text":"For 32 bit production systems: \nSet âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework\\AllowStrongNameBypass\" to a âDWORDâ value of â0â.\nOn 64-bit production systems:\nSet âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework\\ AllowStrongNameBypassâ and âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\.NETFramework\\ AllowStrongNameBypassâ to a âDWORDâ value of â0â.\nOr, obtain documented ISSO risk acceptance for each .Net application installed on the system. \n\nApproval documentation will include complete list of all installed .Net applications, application versions, and acknowledgement of ISSO trust of each installed application.\n","ia_controls":"","rule_title":".NET must be configured to validate strong names on full-trust assemblies.","check_content":"If there is documented ISSO risk acceptance for development systems, this is not a finding.\nFor 32 bit production systems: \nUse regedit to examine the âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFrameworkâ key.  \nOn 64-bit production systems:\nUse regedit to examine both the âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\.NETFrameworkâ and âHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\.NETFrameworkâ keys.\nIf the \"AllowStrongNameBypass\" value does not exist, or if the âDWORDâ value is set to â1â, this is a finding.\n\nDocumentation must include a complete list of installed .Net applications, application versions, and acknowledgement that ISSO trusts each installed application.\n\nIf application versions installed on the system do not match approval documentation, this is a finding.\n\n","group_id":"V-225231","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:def:225231","href":"U_MS_DotNet_Framework_4-0_V2R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-225231","mitigations":"","comments":null,"uuid":"B57CE35B-6BF8-1014-B0C9-DA8C579087B4","legacy_ids":["SV-40977","V-30935"],"documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-225231r961038","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"stig_uuid":"B57BEE89-6BF8-1014-9327-CACC62D6F338","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-225231r961038_rule","discussion":"The \"bypassTrustedAppStrongNames\" setting specifies whether the bypass feature that avoids validating strong names for full-trust assemblies is enabled. By default the bypass feature is enabled in .Net 4, therefore strong names are not validated for correctness when the assembly/program is loaded. Not validating strong names provides a faster application load time but at the expense of performing certificate validation. \n\nFull trust assemblies are .Net applications launched from the local host. Strong names are digital signatures tied to .Net applications/assemblies.  .Net 4 considers applications installed locally to be fully trusted by default and grants these applications full permissions to access host resources. \n\nThe bypass feature applies to any assembly signed with a strong name and having the following characteristics:\n\n    Fully trusted without the StrongName evidence (for example, has MyComputer zone evidence).\n\n    Loaded into a fully trusted AppDomain.\n\n    Loaded from a location under the ApplicationBase property of that AppDomain.\n\n    Not delay-signed.\n\nNot validating the certificates used to sign strong name assemblies will provide a faster application load time, but falsely assumes that signatures used to sign the application are to be implicitly trusted.  Not validating strong name certificates introduces an integrity risk to the system.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000175","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4213","severity":"medium"},{"severity":"low","reference_identifier":"4213","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","discussion":"CAS policy is .NET runtime version-specific.  In .NET Framework version 4, CAS policy is disabled by default however; it can be re-enabled by using the NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy setting on a per application basis. Caspol.exe is provided by Microsoft to set security policy on .Net applications prior to version 4.0. This requirement does not apply to the caspol.exe assembly or other assemblies provided with the Windows OS or the Windows Secure Host Baseline (SHB).\n\nWhen invoking the NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy setting in .NET 4, earlier versions of the .NET Framework CAS policy will become active therefore previous .NET STIG guidance that applies to the reactivated versions must also be applied. \n\nFailure to apply applicable versions of STIG guidance can result in the loss of system confidentiality, integrity or availability.  ","rule_id_src":"SV-225232r1050651_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"B57BEE89-6BF8-1014-9327-CACC62D6F338","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id":"SV-225232r1050651","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":["SV-40979","V-30937"],"uuid":"B57CEC20-6BF8-1014-9EEC-FACEFDE1B582","comments":null,"mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-225232","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:def:225232","href":"U_MS_DotNet_Framework_4-0_V2R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval2.xml"},"group_id":"V-225232","check_content":"The infrastructure to enable Code Access Security (CAS) exists only in .NET Framework 2.x - 4.x.\n\nThe requirement is Not Applicable (NA) for .NET Framework &gt; 4.x.\n\n(Note: The infrastructure is deprecated and is not receiving servicing or security fixes.)\n\nOpen Windows explorer and search for all *.exe.config files. This requirement does not apply to the caspol.exe assembly or other assemblies provided with the Windows OS or the Windows Secure Host Baseline (SHB).\n\nTo find relevant files, run the FINDSTR command from an elevated (admin) command prompt: \nFINDSTR /i /s \"NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy\" c:\\*.exe.config \n\nThis command will search all .\"exe.config\" files on the c: drive partition for the \"LegacySecurityPolicy\" setting. Repeat the command for each drive partition on the system.\n\nIf the .NET application configuration file uses the legacy policy element, and .NET STIG guidance that covers these legacy versions has not been applied, this is a finding.\n","rule_title":".Net applications that invoke NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy must apply previous versions of .NET STIG guidance.","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"The infrastructure to enable CAS exists only in .NET Framework 2.x - 4.x.\n\nThe requirement is Not Applicable (NA) for .NET Framework &gt; 4.x.\n\n(Note: The infrastructure is deprecated and is not receiving servicing or security fixes.)\n\nApply the .NET Framework Security Checklist for .Net versions 1 through 3.5 when using the NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy setting.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:54\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (.Net applications that invoke NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy must apply previous versions of .NET STIG guidance.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523201 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : .Net applications that invoke NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy must apply previous versions of .NET STIG guidance.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523201 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy@enabled from all .exe.config files\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/runtime/NetFx40_LegacySecurityPolicy/@enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523201 (xmlfilecontent_state)\nState Comment           : XML value not equal to 'true'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value_of' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'true'\n","rule_version":"APPNET0064","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516","id":"V-225232"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0"},{"severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4213","group_title":"SRG-APP-000431","discussion":"In the .NET Framework version 3.5 and earlier versions, if an application assembly loaded code/objects from a remote location, that assembly would run partially trusted with a permissions grant set that depended on the zone in which it was loaded. For example, if an assembly was loaded from a web site, it was loaded into the Internet zone and granted the Internet permission set. In other words, it was executed in an Internet sandbox.\n\nIf the same program is run in the .NET Framework version 4, an exception is thrown which effectively states; either explicitly create a sandbox for the assembly or run it in full trust.\n\nThe &lt;loadFromRemoteSources&gt; element specifies the assemblies that run partially trusted in earlier versions of the .NET Framework will be run fully trusted in the .NET Framework 4.\n\nIf loadFromRemoteSources is set to true, the remotely loaded application code is granted full trust.  This could create an integrity vulnerability on the system.  The required method to address this is to explicitly create a sandboxed environment for the remotely loaded code to run in rather than allowing remotely loaded code to run with full trust.\n\nThe appropriate level of trust must be established prior to enabling the loading of remote code in .Net 4 applications and that code must be run in a controlled environment.  The following is an example of the use of loadFromRemoteSources.\n\n&lt;configuration&gt;\n&lt;runtime&gt;\n    &lt;loadFromRemoteSources enabled=\"true\" \"https://my.dodorg.gov\" /&gt;\n    &lt;loadFromRemoteSources enabled=\"true\" \"https://192.168.0.*\" /&gt;\n    &lt;loadFromRemoteSources enabled=\"false\" \"*\" /&gt;\n&lt;/runtime&gt;\n&lt;/configuration&gt;","rule_id_src":"SV-225233r1117179_rule","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"B57BEE89-6BF8-1014-9327-CACC62D6F338","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-002530"],"rule_id":"SV-225233r1117179","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":["SV-41010","V-30968"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","uuid":"B57CF590-6BF8-1014-987B-9E55CD40B2E0","group_id_src":"V-225233","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_DotNet_Framework_4-0_V2R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:def:225233"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-225233","check_content":"Open Windows explorer and search for *.exe.config.\n\nSearch each config file found for the \"loadFromRemoteSources\" element.\n\nIf the loadFromRemoteSources element is enabled  \n(\"loadFromRemoteSources enabled = true\"), and the remotely loaded application is not run in a sandboxed environment, or if OS based software controls, such as AppLocker or Software Security Policies, are not utilized, this is a finding.\n","rule_title":"Trust must be established prior to enabling the loading of remote code in .Net 4.","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","fix_text":".Net application code loaded from a remote source must be run in a controlled environment.  \n\nA controlled environment consists of a sandbox, such as running in an Internet Explorer host environment or employing OS based software access controls, such as AppLocker or Software Security Policies, when application design permits.  \n\nObtain documented IAO approvals for all remotely loaded code.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:54\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Trust must be established prior to enabling the loading of remote code in .Net 4.)\nResult Analysis         :        C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x64.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\ScenarioEngine.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x86.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\setup.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\SetupARP.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\LandingPage.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523301 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Trust must be established prior to enabling the loading of remote code in .Net 4.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523301 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather loadFromRemoteSources@enabled from all .exe.config files\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\setup.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x64.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x86.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\LandingPage.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\ScenarioEngine.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\SetupARP.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523301 (xmlfilecontent_state)\nState Comment           : XML value not equal to 'true'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value_of' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x64.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64'\n                        : filename equals 'FixSqlRegistryKey_x64.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\ScenarioEngine.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64'\n                        : filename equals 'ScenarioEngine.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x86.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64'\n                        : filename equals 'FixSqlRegistryKey_x86.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\setup.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022'\n                        : filename equals 'setup.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\SetupARP.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64'\n                        : filename equals 'SetupARP.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\LandingPage.exe.config'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64'\n                        : filename equals 'LandingPage.exe.config'\n                        : xpath equals '/configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled'\n                        : value_of equals 'true'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x64.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\ScenarioEngine.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\FixSqlRegistryKey_x86.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\setup.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\SetupARP.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n                        : C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\SQL2022\\x64\\LandingPage.exe.config xpath = /configuration/runtime/loadFromRemoteSources/@enabled = 'true' failed test of 'case insensitive not equal' compared to 'true' \n","group_tree":{"id":"V-225233","title":"SRG-APP-000431"},"rule_version":"APPNET0065","status":"open","weight":"10.0"},{"security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"B57BEE89-6BF8-1014-9327-CACC62D6F338","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-225234r1188289_rule","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","discussion":"The .Net framework can be configured to utilize a different proxy or altogether bypass the default proxy settings in the client's browser.  This may lead to the framework using a proxy that is not approved for use.  If the proxy is malicious, this could lead to a loss of application integrity and confidentiality.","severity":"low","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4213","uuid":"B57CFDF0-6BF8-1014-A1D6-AA7D1CDF1244","comments":null,"mitigations":"","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":["SV-41014","V-30972"],"rule_id":"SV-225234r1188289","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_title":".NET default proxy settings must be reviewed and approved.","group_id":"V-225234","check_content":"Open Windows explorer and search for all \"*.exe.config\" and \"machine.config\" files.\n\nThe referenced file is in the WinSxS directory (original source component file used when the Windows component was installed).\n\nIf the files under WinSxS are read-only and cannot be modified, this is not a finding.\n\nSearch each file for the \"defaultProxy\" element.\n\n&lt;defaultProxy\n  enabled=\"true|false\"\n  useDefaultCredentials=\"true|false\"\n  &lt;bypasslist&gt; â¦ &lt;/bypasslist&gt;\n  &lt;proxy&gt; â¦ &lt;/proxy&gt;\n  &lt;module&gt; â¦ &lt;/module&gt;\n/&gt;\n\nIf the \"defaultProxy\" setting \"enabled=false\" or if the \"bypasslist\", \"module\", or \"proxy\" child elements have configuration entries and there are no documented approvals from the authorizing official (AO), this is a finding.\n\nIf the \"defaultProxy\" element is empty or ifÂ \"useSystemDefault =TrueâÂ then the framework is using default browser settings, this is not a finding.","mitigation_control":"","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:def:225234","href":"U_MS_DotNet_Framework_4-0_V2R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval2.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-225234","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516","id":"V-225234"},"rule_version":"APPNET0066","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:54\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     true (If the defaultProxy setting enabled=false this is a finding)\nTest                    :     true (DefaultProxy bypasslist should not exist)\nTest                    :     true (DefaultProxy module should not exist)\nTest                    :     true (DefaultProxy proxy should not exist)\nTest                    :   true (If the 'defaultProxy' element is empty or if 'useSystemDefault =True' then the framework is using default browser settings, this is not a finding.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523401 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the defaultProxy setting enabled=false this is a finding\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523401 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather the defaultProxy enabled value\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/system.net[1]/defaultProxy[1]/@enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523401 (xmlfilecontent_state)\nState Comment           : XML value not equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value_of' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'false'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523402 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DefaultProxy bypasslist should not exist\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523403 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather the defaultProxy/bypasslist value\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/system.net/defaultProxy/bypasslist/@*'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523403 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DefaultProxy module should not exist\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523404 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather the defaultProxy/module value\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/system.net/defaultProxy/module/@*'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523404 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DefaultProxy proxy should not exist\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523405 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather the defaultProxy/proxy value\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/system.net/defaultProxy/proxy/@*'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:tst:22523405 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : If the 'defaultProxy' element is empty or if 'useSystemDefault =True' then the framework is using default browser settings, this is not a finding.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:obj:22523406 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather the defaultProxy - proxy - usesystemdefault value\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'xpath' must be equal to '/configuration/system.net[1]/defaultProxy[1]/proxy[1]/@usesystemdefault'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.dotnet:ste:22523402 (xmlfilecontent_state)\nState Comment           : XML value of 'True'.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value_of' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'true'\n","ia_controls":"","fix_text":"Open Windows explorer and search for all \"*.exe.config\" and \"machine.config\" files.\n\nSearch each file for the \"defaultProxy\" element.\n\nClear the values contained in the \"defaultProxy\" element, and the \"bypasslist\", \"module\", and \"proxy\" child elements.\n\nThe IAO must provide documented approvals of any non-default proxy servers.","false_positives":""},{"fix_text":"Open Windows explorer and search for all .NET config files including application config files (*.exe.config).\n\nExamine the configuration settings for \n&lt;etwEnable enabled=\"false\" /&gt;.\n\nEnable ETW Tracing by setting the etwEnable flag to \"true\" or obtain documented IAO approvals.","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","group_tree":{"id":"V-225235","title":"SRG-APP-000095"},"rule_version":"APPNET0067","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:54\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Event tracing for Windows (ETW) for Common Language Runtime events is enabled for application configiguration files)\nTest                    :   true (Event tracing for Windows (ETW) for Common Language Runtime events is enabled for machine configiguration files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.dotnet:tst:1200 (xmlfilecontent_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Event tracing for Windows (ETW) for Common Language Runtime events is enabled for application configiguration files\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.dotnet:obj:1200 (xmlfilecontent_object)\nObject Comment          : *.exe.config etwEnable/@enabled true or nonexistant\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, at least one of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\mmc.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\v4.0.30319\\cvtres.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Update Cache\\KB5065221\\GDR\\SETUP.EXE.CONFIG'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft SQL Server\\160\\Setup Bootstrap\\Update Cache\\KB5035432\\GDR\\x64\\FIXSQLREGISTRYKEY_X86.EXE.CONFIG'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Windows\\AzureArcSetup\\ArcSetup\\AzureArcSetup.exe.config'\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\assemb